      "message": "[error] Line 312: 🔴 `publishedCrlId_.exchange()` only makes the id write atomic; it does not serialize the cancel/put sequence or prevent older CRLs from winning a race. `startSync()` and `revokeDevice()` are explicitly expected to run on different threads, so an older `publishCurrentCrl()` call can exchange/compute first, then publish after a newer revocation has already been put, leaving the superseded CRL active or even cancelling the newer one. Protect the whole publish decision with a mutex and track the current CRL update time/id so calls with an older `getUpdateTime()` are ignored before cancelling or putting.",
